# Build context sent to the Docker daemon on EVERY build, backend or
# frontend. Without this file that was the entire repo - measured at
# 226 MB here, dominated by frontend/node_modules (215 MB) plus .git
# (3 MB) - read off the Pi's SD card each time, before any layer
# caching even gets a chance to help.
#
# Both Dockerfiles copy narrowly (backend/requirements.txt,
# backend/app, frontend/, docker/nginx*), so everything excluded below
# is genuinely unused by either build.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# node_modules - the big one, and not just a size problem.
# docker/frontend.Dockerfile runs `npm ci` in its own cached layer and
# THEN does `COPY frontend/ ./`. If a node_modules directory exists on
# the host it lands directly on top of the one npm ci just built - and
# on this Pi that would be armv7 host binaries overwriting the
# container's, or vice versa. Native modules would be the wrong
# architecture. Excluding it keeps the ci layer authoritative.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
**/node_modules

# Build output - regenerated inside the image by `npm run build`.
# Copying the host's stale dist in only to overwrite it wastes
# context and risks leaving orphaned files from an older build.
**/dist
**/.vite
*.tsbuildinfo

# Git history. Nothing in either build reads it, and it grows forever.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Python caches and local virtualenvs - wrong architecture in an
# image anyway.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.venv
**/venv

# LIVE DATA - must never be baked into an image. This is the running
# SQLite DB and config.json (which holds auth tokens and API keys) on
# the Pi; in the running stack it comes from a mounted volume, not
# from the build.
backend/data
**/*.db

# Secrets. .env.example is committed and harmless, but the real .env
# has no business in a layer.
.env
.env.local
**/.env

# Docs, the marketing site, and the frontend test suite. None are
# referenced by either Dockerfile - tsconfig builds only `src` and
# `vite.config.ts`, so `tsc -b && vite build` never reads tests/.
docs
site
frontend/tests
frontend/scripts
*.md
LICENSE

# Local compose overrides and editor/OS noise
docker-compose.override.yml
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.log
